{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/10631","createdAt":"2026-10-02T02:12:29Z","decision":"request_changes","decisionDigest":"sha256:37a584c22aaee245a380f6ae33ba89d9ff6bd4e203679e1437de7b87be8291f6","decisionId":"rdec-b026cdca1a2c9b005fe8be5df126a290","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:2c95bf6fcc9ccb823cbf64daeee0165ef2574b5e9cfdfac0b415e3ec0cc9c54b","packageIdentity":"epkg-f4bb61cd145f99129d783ed768c40c3d1d5cab1e5ed85fd33df016de27461e23","prNumber":"10631","reason":"Changes needed for the stated goal (our comment on #10601, re-checked on this mirror). The change is behaviour-compatible: heights are identical at base and head in the real qml6 engine. But it does not remove the quadratic walk: QML tracks every property read inside the functions a binding calls, and rowListHeight / dmenuRowListHeight still read displayModel.count and every row, so a 231-row open still takes 232 height passes over 27,027 row visits (KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC stays open). The new test checks source text and a JavaScript model, not the QML engine, so it passes while the cost is unchanged. It now runs in the audit and passes, and we leave it unmapped on purpose: it states no behaviour of an existing requirement, and the requirement it aims at, a bound on the menu-open cost that KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC asks for, does not hold at this head. Append the rows in one model update, or take the height out of the binding. The rowsLoaded=false serial bump is necessary and correct. Advisory: we cannot approve for the maintainers.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
